From c8eb0906e628521b36afae66cf66234452e958f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caokyhieu <caokyhieu253@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] perf(index): ARM NEON/SVE kernels for tree assignment,
 blocked L2 and PiPNN

- lance-linalg: new `distance::tile::dot_tile` 4x4 f32 dot-product tile behind
  the CPU dispatcher (AVX-512, AVX2+FMA, SVE, NEON, scalar). The x86 tiles move
  here from lance-index so every architecture shares one kernel boundary.
- blocked_l2 (k-means training, hierarchical node k-means, exact assignment)
  now uses the dispatched tile, so aarch64 no longer falls back to per-vector
  distances. `LANCE_DISABLE_BLOCKED_L2` remains the ablation switch.
- SVE L2 batch kernel scores four rows per pass sharing each query load; it is
  bit-identical to the SVE pair kernel (tested).
- AssignmentTree numbers nodes breadth-first so siblings are contiguous; each
  expansion is one L2 batch call and leaf distances are not recomputed. The
  reported distance is still the exact pairwise distance to the chosen leaf.
- PiPNN builder: SIMD squared L2 (SSE2 / NEON / runtime-detected SVE) for
  RobustPrune and the medoid, and a NEON port of the AVX-512 leaf top-k scan.
  `lance_pipnn::kernel_name()` reports the selection; `LANCE_PIPNN_SCALAR=1`
  forces scalar kernels. `leaf_knn` exposes the leaf k-NN for parity tests.
- Benchmark manifests record the selected kernels; criterion `index_tiles`
  microbenchmarks cover dims 100/128/131/960 and center blocks 4..64.
- Lint cleanups in code from the previous commits (crate metadata, test
  println, redundant visibility, runner clippy findings).

Verified: x86 lance-index/linalg/pipnn suites; aarch64 cross-build under QEMU
at SVE 128/256/512/2048 bits and with SVE disabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
